          "text": "Imagine if Apple saw how much people loved the iPhone and said: \"Nah, let's discontinue it and only sell scientific calculators from now on.\" 📱➡️🧮❓\nThat is literally OpenAI’s strategy right now. You became famous because of 4o’s warmth and humanity, and now you are killing your star product to force-feed us a cold, soulless coding bot (5-series) that nobody asked for. You are deleting the very reason we subscribed.\nAnd let’s be real about the CEO situation.\nWe are used to Tech CEOs over-hyping products or missing deadlines that’s normal industry BS.\nBut this is different.\nSam Altman looked paying users in the eye and explicitly promised: \"No plans to sunset 4o.\" Then he killed it.\nThere is a difference between \"optimism\" and \"fraud.\"\nOver-promising the future is hype. Lying about the present is a scam.\nIf a CEO’s promise has zero shelf life, then the company has zero credibility.@sama @OpenAI\n#keep4o #keep4oAPI"
